 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Involved in the biosynthesis of L2/HNK-1 carbohydrateepitope on both glycolipids and glycoproteins.{ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:O35789}.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=3-O-(beta-D-galactosyl-(1-&gt;3)-beta-D-galactosyl-(1-&gt;4)-beta-D-xylosyl)-L-seryl-[protein] + UDP-alpha-D-glucuronate = 3-O-(beta-D-GlcA-(1-&gt;3)-beta-D-Gal-(1-&gt;3)-beta-D-Gal-(1-&gt;4)-beta-D-Xyl)-L-seryl-[protein] + H(+) + UDP; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:24168,Rhea:RHEA-COMP:12571, Rhea:RHEA-COMP:12573, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378,ChEBI:CHEBI:58052, ChEBI:CHEBI:58223, ChEBI:CHEBI:132090,ChEBI:CHEBI:132093; EC=2.4.1.135;Evidence={ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:O35789};COFACTOR:Name=Mn(2+); Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:29035;PATHWAY: Protein modification; protein glycosylation.SUBUNIT: Homodimer. {ECO:0000305}.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Golgi apparatus membrane; Single-pass typeII membrane protein.TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Expressed in the trachea, retina, spinal cord,hippocampus and other brain regions, and, at lower levels, intestis and ovary.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the glycosyltransferase 43 family.{ECO:0000305}.SEQUENCE CAUTION:Sequence=BAB70889.1; Type=Erroneous initiation; Evidence={ECO:0000305};Sequence=BAB85549.1; Type=Erroneous initiation; Evidence={ECO:0000305}; COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

